+## GLM take-over, decided then copied (TF_GLM_DECIDE_THEN_COPY)
+
+`families/glm5_next/cuda/engine.py`'s `GlmEngine._take_over_decided` (a request that takes the caches over works out
+which kept snapshots stay within the budget from their sizes, drops the rest without a copy and clones only the ones
+that stay; the same snapshots stay as before, so a fresh conversation after a long one no longer clones every kept
+state first and runs out of memory) is MiaAI-Lab's
+[GLM-5.3-Flash EXL3 2x DGX Spark recipe](https://github.com/MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-2x-DGX-Sparks-TensorFold/tree/33b50fde06fd7ea604cbc6a663880068ab1e2ee4)
+patch 0078-glm-take-over-decide-then-copy's `_take_over` (v1.8), written by
+[m-naoki-m](https://github.com/m-naoki-m) in
+[pull request #71](https://github.com/MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-2x-DGX-Sparks-TensorFold/pull/71) (commit
+[`b9fa2ff`](https://github.com/MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-2x-DGX-Sparks-TensorFold/commit/b9fa2ff98a78b1a6e9fc9d349de9757c3b27cbd5))
+and applied by MiaAI-Lab as contributed; m-naoki-m also proposed it to TensorFold as
+[pull request #421](https://github.com/ashhart/TensorFold/pull/421). Under the recipe's Apache License 2.0 (see
+[the license text](LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt)). Changes in the port: the recipe replaces `_take_over`'s walk, and here
+it sits beside it as `_take_over_decided`, used only with `TF_GLM_DECIDE_THEN_COPY=1` (`decide_then_copy`, read at
+each take-over; unset or 0: the walk as before); its calls pass the drafter only when there is one, as this tree's
+`_take_over` does (the patch passes `drafter=drafter`). It acts on the one-stream path (`--parallel 1`) and the
+label scores' prefill; under `--parallel` the pool keeps prompts in place and `_take_over` is not called.
